<title>USA: Woodland Hills, Pa., approves property tax hike.</title>
<headline>Woodland Hills, Pa., approves property tax hike.</headline>
<dateline>WOODLAND HILLS, Pa. 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Woodland Hills, Pa.'s school district has approved a property tax increase, sparking complaints from parents who argue the extra money is not improving education.</p>
<p>The board approved the increase, which averages about $75 per year for homeowners.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
